  the earlier work or a work "based on" the earlier work.

  A "covered work" means either the unmodified Program or a work based
  on the Program.

  To "propagate" a work means to do anything with it that, without
  permission, would make you directly or indirectly liable for
  infringement, excluding private distribution to members of the same
  household.  To "convey" a work means any kind of propagation that
  enables other parties to make copies of the work.  The second
  interaction with others requires only passive reception; "interact"
  through a computer network, with no transfer of a copy, is not
  conveying.

  The "Corresponding Source" for a work in object code form means all
  the source code needed to generate, install, and run the object code
  and to modify the work, including scripts to control those activities.
  However, it does not include the work's System Libraries, or general
  purpose tools or generally available free programs which are used
  unmodified in performing those activities but which are not part of
  the work.  For example, Corresponding Source includes interface
  definition files associated with source files for the work, and the
  source code for shared libraries and dynamically linked subprograms
  that the work is designed to require, or specifically designed to use,
  such an interface or shared library, provided the source code for the
  shared library is included in the Corresponding Source.

